1
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:14,680
Sunday, April 29, 1945, one week before the end of World War II in Europe.  

2
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:21,960
45th Infantry Division of the Seventh United States Army liberates Dachau, the first camp  

3
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:28,760
concentration camp built by the Nazi government. Soldiers not only smell human excrement,  

4
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:34,200
but also decomposing bodies, which makes many of them cry or vomit when  

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:41,080
find piles of incredibly malnourished corpses, more than 30 train cars full of  

6
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:46,960
thousands of corpses and 30 thousand survivors, most of them severely emaciated,  

7
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:53,280
that look like walking skeletons. Some of them were even subjected to cruel and painful  

8
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:59,440
pseudomedical experiments carried out by one of the most sadistic and morally depraved Nazi doctors  

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,400
corrupt. His name is Sigmund Rascher.

10
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:12,600
Sigmund Rascher was born on February 12, 1909 in Munich, then part of the German Empire.  

11
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,920
He was the third son of Dr. Hanns-August Rascher, whose brother was the musician Sigurd  

12
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:29,555
Rascher. His father was a committed supporter of the anthroposophist Rudolf Steiner and in fact in 1921  

13
00:01:29,555 --> 00:01:32,560
participated in Steiner's first medical course. The young Sigmund attended the  

14
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:39,940
First Waldorf School in Stuttgart, a school based on the anthroposophical approach  

15
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:44,800
Steiner's approach to education. He was influenced by Ehrenfried Pfeiffer, who believed in  

16
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:51,720
the influence of cosmic rhythms on life processes. He completed his secondary education  

17
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:59,440
in Konstanz in 1930 and the same year he began studying medicine at the University of Freiburg.

18
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:05,760
On January 30, 1933, Adolf Hitler was appointed Chancellor of Germany by the  

19
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:11,080
President Paul von Hindenburg and, a few months later, Sigmund Rascher joined  

20
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:16,800
to the Nazi Party. After completing his preliminary examination, he worked for his father,  

21
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:24,800
now divorced, in Basel, Switzerland, and continued his medical studies there. In October 1934,  

22
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:30,080
He returned to Germany to study at the Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich.  

23
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:38,600
In 1936 he passed the state medical examination there, obtained his doctorate and joined the SA.

24
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:44,920
That same year he met his future wife, Karoline Diehl, a former cabaret singer,  

25
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:52,160
who had been widowed in 1929, since her first husband, the theatre director Oskar Diehl,  

26
00:02:52,160 --> 00:03:00,080
had passed away. Karoline, who was born in 1893, was 15 years older than Rascher and had  

27
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:05,600
valuable contacts at the highest levels of politics. In the early days of the Party  

28
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:11,880
Nazi, helped Heinrich Himmler and from then on maintained contact with the future Reichsführer of  

29
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:18,720
the SS. Thanks to her close relationship with Himmler, who was allegedly her former lover,  

30
00:03:18,720 --> 00:03:24,640
was able to offer Rascher opportunities for career advancement within the Nazi state.  

31
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:32,520
At his recommendation, Himmler received Rascher in person for the first time in April 1939.

32
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:38,800
A week after his first meeting with Himmler, Rascher presented a document entitled  

33
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:44,560
"Report on the development and solution of some of the tasks assigned to the Reichsführer  

34
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:52,200
during a discussion held on April 24, 1939." Rascher became involved in the test  

35
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:57,800
of a plant extract as a cancer treatment. Professor Kurt Blome,  

36
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:02,840
Deputy Minister of Health and Plenipotentiary for Cancer Research,  

37
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:07,480
was in favor of testing the extract on mice, but Rascher insisted  

38
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:14,240
use human test subjects. Himmler sided with Rascher and established  

39
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:19,120
a human cancer testing station at the Dachau concentration camp.

40
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:26,920
Dachau was the first concentration camp created by the Nazi government in March 1933,  

41
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:32,720
less than two months after Hitler became chancellor. During the first year,  

42
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:37,280
The camp had a capacity of 5,000 prisoners. At first,  

43
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:41,920
The internees were mainly German communists, social democrats,  

44
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:48,120
trade unionists and other political opponents of the Nazi regime. However, over time, other  

45
00:04:48,120 --> 00:04:54,640
Groups were also interned at Dachau, such as Jehovah's Witnesses, Roma and Sinti,  

46
00:04:54,640 --> 00:05:01,000
homosexuals, repeat offenders, as well as the so-called "asocials", whom the  

47
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:06,160
regime imprisoned them because they could not or would not find paid employment.  

48
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:12,800
During the early years, relatively few Jews were interned at Dachau, and in general,  

49
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:18,800
They only ended up inside if they belonged to one of the groups mentioned or had served sentences.  

50
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:25,880
from prison after being convicted of violating the Nuremberg Laws of 1935,  

51
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:35,040
who incorporated Nazi ideas about race into legislation. In early 1937, the SS,  

52
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:40,840
Using prisoner labor, they began to build a large complex of buildings in the  

53
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:46,640
land of the original camp. The prisoners were forced to do this work,  

54
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:51,600
starting with the destruction of the old munitions factory, under conditions  

55
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:59,080
terrible. Construction was officially completed in mid-August 1938.

56
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:05,960
One month before World War II, which began on September 1, 1939 with the invasion  

57
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:12,360
A German from Poland, Rascher had been recruited into the Luftwaffe, the German air force.

58
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:18,000
Due to Rascher's servile and ingratiating treatment of Himmler, his connections were so  

59
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:24,120
so strong that practically all of his superiors trembled with fear before the scheming Rascher,  

60
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:28,680
who consequently occupied a position of enormous power. 

61
00:06:28,680 --> 00:06:37,560
In October 1939, Rascher transferred from the SA to the SS and to marry Karoline he needed  

62
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:43,720
Himmler's approval. This was part of the strict control and regulation of private life  

63
00:06:43,720 --> 00:06:49,240
of the SS members, as Himmler intended to ensure that their marriages would be  

64
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:55,520
conform to the racial and ideological principles of the Nazi regime. Due to Karoline's age,  

65
00:06:55,520 --> 00:07:00,800
Himmler was initially opposed to the two marrying, as it was not expected that  

66
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:07,080
a marriage with numerous children would occur. The Nazi regime encouraged the birth of children  

67
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:12,560
considered "racially valuable" to increase the "Aryan" population of Germany.

68
00:07:12,560 --> 00:07:20,480
In 1939, Karoline and Rascher had an illegitimate child and when Karoline reported once again  

69
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:26,240
that she was pregnant again, Himmler finally authorized the marriage, which took place in July  

70
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:34,720
1942. Himmler supported the couple and, after having their second child, transferred 165 marks to them.  

71
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:41,440
of the Reich every month. He also sent them packages with fruit, chocolate, and other gifts. Karoline  

72
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:48,120
He returned the favor with family photos and asked for Rascher to be given a better job. Rascher  

73
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:53,480
He also frequently wrote to Himmler requesting money, tax reductions,  

74
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:59,440
fresh fruit, furniture, fruit juices, a new apartment and even slave maids.

75
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:05,120
Rascher suggested that high-altitude and low-altitude experiments be performed.  

76
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:10,840
pressure in humans. While attending an aeronautical medicine course in Munich,  

77
00:08:10,840 --> 00:08:16,280
He wrote a letter to Himmler in which he said that his course included research on flights to  

78
00:08:16,280 --> 00:08:21,840
high altitude and regretted that human trials could not be carried out,  

79
00:08:21,840 --> 00:08:29,160
since such experiments were very dangerous and no one volunteered for them. Rascher  

80
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:35,600
He asked Himmler to make human subjects available to him, stating quite frankly  

81
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:41,240
that the experiments could prove fatal, but that previous tests carried out with  

82
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:46,960
monkeys had not been satisfactory. The letter was answered by Rudolf Brandt,  

83
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:52,360
Himmler's adjutant, who informed Rascher that prisoners would be made available.

84
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:58,400
Rascher wrote to Brandt to ask for permission to carry out his experiments at Dachau,  

85
00:08:58,400 --> 00:09:02,520
and plans for the experiments were developed at a conference  

86
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:10,120
early 1942, attended by Rascher and members of the Luftwaffe Medical Service.  

87
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:15,680
Experiments were carried out in the spring and summer of the same year, using a chamber  

88
00:09:15,680 --> 00:09:22,000
portable pressure chamber supplied by the Luftwaffe. The victims were locked in the chamber,  

89
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:28,200
whose internal pressure was reduced to a level corresponding to very high altitudes. The  

90
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:33,640
pressure could be altered very quickly, which allowed Rascher to simulate the conditions that  

91
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:39,520
would experience a pilot in free fall from an altitude without oxygen. After seeing a report of  

92
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:46,040
one of the fatal experiments, Himmler commented that if a subject survived such treatment,  

93
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:51,320
should be "pardoned" to life imprisonment. Rascher, however, responded to Himmler  

94
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:56,160
that the victims to date had been simply Poles and Soviets,  

95
00:09:56,160 --> 00:10:01,880
and believed that they should not be given any kind of amnesty. Of the 200 subjects,  

96
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:07,640
80 died directly from the experiment and the rest were murdered.

97
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:12,600
Rascher also carried out so-called "freezing experiments" on behalf of  

98
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:18,920
the Luftwaffe with 300 test subjects without their consent. The experiments were carried out  

99
00:10:18,920 --> 00:10:24,280
carried out at Dachau after the high-altitude tests had been completed. The purpose  

100
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:29,560
was to determine the best way to warm up the German pilots who had been forced  

101
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:35,040
descended into the North Sea and suffered hypothermia. Rascher's victims were  

102
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:41,320
forced to remain naked outdoors in freezing weather for 14 hours or kept  

103
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:46,880
in a tank of ice water for three hours, measuring their pulse and internal temperature through  

104
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:52,400
of a series of electrodes. Then attempts were made to warm the victims by different methods,  

105
00:10:52,400 --> 00:10:57,640
the most common and successful one is immersion in hot water; at least one witness,  

106
00:10:57,640 --> 00:11:02,840
assistant in some of these proceedings, later testified that some victims were  

107
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:09,240
thrown into boiling water to reheat. Himmler attended some of the experiments  

108
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:14,440
and told Rascher that he should go to the North Sea region and find out how people  

109
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:20,920
common there warmed victims of extreme cold. Himmler is reported to have said that he thought  

110
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:26,960
that "a fisherwoman could take her half-frozen husband to bed and revive him that way  

111
00:11:26,960 --> 00:11:32,440
way" and added that everyone believed that "animal heat" had a different effect  

112
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:39,080
to artificial heat. Four Roma women were sent from the concentration camp  

113
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:45,640
from Ravensbrück and an attempt was made to warm him by placing the hypothermic victim between two naked women. 

114
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:51,800
Rascher also experimented with the effects of Polygal, a substance made from pectin.  

115
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:58,120
beetroot and apple, which helped blood clotting. He predicted that the preventive use of  

116
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:03,760
Polygal tablets would reduce bleeding from gunshot wounds sustained during combat or  

117
00:12:03,760 --> 00:12:10,160
during surgery. Subjects were given a Polygal tablet and shot in the neck  

118
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:16,520
or chest, or their limbs were amputated without anesthesia. Rascher published an article about  

119
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:22,680
their experience with the use of Polygal, without detailing the nature of the human trials and also  

120
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:29,560
He created a company to manufacture the substance, whose staff was made up of prisoners.

121
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:36,400
Between July and September 1944, other experiments on human beings were carried out at Dachau.  

122
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:42,440
humans, in which prisoners were subjected to tests on the potability of seawater.  

123
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:48,120
Doctors forced about 90 Roma prisoners to drink only seawater and,  

124
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:54,160
At the same time, they were deprived of food. The Roma prisoners became so dehydrated that,  

125
00:12:54,160 --> 00:13:00,560
It is said that they would lick the floor after scrubbing it to get a drop of fresh water.  

126
00:13:00,560 --> 00:13:07,160
experiments caused enormous pain and suffering and resulted in serious bodily injury. 

127
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:12,520
Rascher, who also allegedly collected human skin to make saddles,  

128
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:20,320
was one of Himmler's favorites, but this was about to change in late 1943.

129
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:26,960
In an attempt to please Himmler by demonstrating that population growth could be accelerated if  

130
00:13:26,960 --> 00:13:32,880
the reproductive age of women was extended, Rascher made public the fact that his wife,  

131
00:13:32,880 --> 00:13:39,040
Karoline had given birth to three children even after she turned 48,  

132
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:46,160
and Himmler used a photograph of Rascher's family as propaganda material. However,  

133
00:13:46,160 --> 00:13:53,120
During her fourth "pregnancy", Karoline Rascher was arrested while attempting to kidnap a baby.  

134
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:59,040
A subsequent investigation revealed that her other three children had been bought or kidnapped. 

135
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:05,600
In addition to acting as an accomplice in the kidnappings of the three babies, Rascher was also charged with  

136
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:10,880
financial irregularities, the murder of his former laboratory assistant, and fraud  

137
00:14:10,880 --> 00:14:18,320
scientist. In December 1943, Rascher's laboratory assistant and housekeeper,  

138
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:22,760
Julie Muschler, who had once lived in an apartment with the Raschers,  

139
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:26,560
disappeared during a mountain trip with his partner.

140
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:33,320
When his body was found in April 1944, both Raschers came under strong suspicion.  

141
00:14:33,320 --> 00:14:39,160
of murder. Himmler, enraged that the Raschers had taken advantage of his trust,  

142
00:14:39,160 --> 00:14:45,400
had both of them sent to concentration camps without trial. Sigmund was sent  

143
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:50,600
to Buchenwald and Karoline was sent to Ravensbrück. Both were held  

144
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:57,400
in bunkers designated for special prisoners. Karoline, 51, was executed by hanging in  

145
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:06,360
Ravensbrück at the end of April 1945. Her husband remained in Buchenwald after his arrest in 1944,  

146
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:13,560
until the camp's evacuation in April 1945, and was then taken to Dachau. Sigmund  

147
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:20,360
Rascher was 36 years old when he was executed on April 26 by direct order of Himmler,  

148
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:25,400
just three days before the camp was liberated by American troops.  

149
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:30,960
Rascher was killed by an SS officer who shot him through the door of  

150
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:36,040
observing the cell and the delivery of food and then kicked him  

151
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:42,680
on the body while saying: "Pig, now you have the punishment you deserve."

152
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:52,120
No tears were shed for Sigmund Rascher.

